From: djvalic <djvalic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 20:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ad5x: the language picker offers English and Russian

Kiln OS's list for Settings > Language & Time and the setup wizard's
language step: English and Russian (en, ru), in place of upstream's ten
(it was nine before: en, zh, ja, de, es, it, ru, pt, tr). The image
installs only these two packs (Kiln OS helixscreen.mk), to keep the
rootfs inside its 100 MiB slot. The other languages' translations/*.yml
stay in the source, so one can come back by adding its code here and its
row to the wizard. The wizard's welcome text cycles through the two.

A saved code the list lacks reads as English (index 0), and the locale
of a saved one follows it; patch 0104 also saves it as English at start.
---
 src/system/system_settings_manager.cpp       | 20 ++---
 src/ui/wizard/ui_wizard_language_chooser.cpp |  9 +--
 ui_xml/wizard_language_chooser.xml           | 84 +-------------------
 3 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 104 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/system/system_settings_manager.cpp b/src/system/system_settings_manager.cpp
index bc557c1ff7..e14ffebe25 100644
--- a/src/system/system_settings_manager.cpp
+++ b/src/system/system_settings_manager.cpp
@@ -47,20 +47,12 @@ static int spdlog_level_to_index(spdlog::level::level_enum level) {
 }
 
 // Language options - codes and display names
-// Order: en, en-GB, de, fr, es, ru, pt, it, zh, ja (indices 0-9). A regional
-// variant sits right after its base language and is named in it ("English (UK)").
-// The CJK pair comes last so a build without CJK fonts (HELIX_HAS_CJK=0, the
-// ESP32 firmware) drops it by shortening the list, and every other index keeps
-// its meaning. A saved zh/ja there reads as English. Settings store the code, so
-// an index is never persisted.
-static const char* kLanguageCodes[] = {"en", "en-GB", "de", "fr", "es",
-                                       "ru", "pt",    "it", "zh", "ja"};
-static const int kLanguageCount = HELIX_HAS_CJK ? 10 : 8;
-static const char* kLanguageOptionsText =
-    HELIX_HAS_CJK
-        ? "English\nEnglish (UK)\nDeutsch\nFrançais\nEspañol\nРусский\nPortuguês\nItaliano"
-          "\n中文\n日本語"
-        : "English\nEnglish (UK)\nDeutsch\nFrançais\nEspañol\nРусский\nPortuguês\nItaliano";
+// Order: en, ru. Kiln OS ships only these two packs (image space); the other
+// languages' translations/*.yml stay in the source. A saved code not in this
+// list reads as English. Settings store the code, so an index is never persisted.
+static const char* kLanguageCodes[] = {"en", "ru"};
+static const int kLanguageCount = 2;
+static const char* kLanguageOptionsText = "English\nРусский";
 
 using settings::Scope;
 // Row order is SystemSettingsManager::Key.
